# Credit Cards Module

## Scope

Philippine bank credit card SOA automation. This module must preserve behavior from `automated-tasks/pay-credit-cards` unless explicitly changing product requirements.

## Supported Banks

| Issuer ID | Label | Notes |
| --------- | ----- | ----- |
| `metrobank` | Metrobank | MSOA / SOA Gmail queries |
| `rcbc` | RCBC | FLEX VISA; geometry-ordered PDF lines |
| `bpi` | BPI | Often needs OCR (`BPI_OCR`) |
| `unionbank` | Unionbank | REWARDS VISA patterns |

## SOA Pipeline (service layer)

Order of operations (match legacy `soa-run.ts`):

1. Build month context (`gmailMonthOffset` per card)
2. Gmail search per bank → download PDFs
3. Unlock PDF with card password(s)
4. Parse SOA fields + transactions
5. Write summary PDF to storage (optional download in UI)
6. Upsert `due_entries` from parsed rows
7. Notify via `notification.service` (Telegram PDF + Slack text)
8. Optional: create calendar events via `google-calendar.service`

## Due Entries

- Key: `issuerId` + normalized `cardLast4` + `dueDateYmd`
- Keep latest due date when range runs overlap
- `paidAt` suppresses reminder fingerprints
- `overviewIsPaidLabel` logic for summary PDF "Is paid" column

## Mark Paid

| Input | Behavior |
| ----- | -------- |
| `xxxx - month year - paid` | Text command (Telegram or API) |
| Receipt image | AI vision → amount ≥ minimum due → mark paid |
| `xxxx - month year - unpaid` | Reverse paid state |

Side effects: update due entry, suppress/restore reminder fingerprints, patch calendar events.

## Receipt AI validation

- Gemini 2.5 Flash vision (multi-key rotation) + Groq fallback
- Extract card last-4, amount, bank/wallet from PH e-wallet/bank screenshots
- Amount must meet minimum due (or total when `RECEIPT_REQUIRE_TOTAL_DUE=1`)
- Store uploads in Supabase Storage under `receipts/{userId}/`

## Security

- Card PDF passwords: encrypt at rest; never return in API responses
- Gmail/Calendar tokens: per-user integration record, not global `.env` files in production

## Testing Parity

When porting parsers, compare output against legacy CLI on sample PDFs in `pay-credit-cards/data/downloads/`.

## Skills

Use `/credit-cards` and `/integrations` skills when implementing this module.
